+# TREBLO v1.2.1-rc.5 — Windows build identity hotfix
+
+## Root cause confirmed
+
+`app/build_info.py` hashed `str(path.relative_to(ROOT))`.
+On Windows this contains `\\` path separators; on Linux it contains `/`.
+This made the exact same distribution compute different BUILD_ID values:
+
+- Original POSIX: `e164fd6a744d182a`
+- Original Windows: `bff417203670560c` (as on the supplied screenshot)
+
+## Patch
+
+Use `path.relative_to(ROOT).as_posix()` for hashing on all OS.
+Then restamp frontend `ui/app.js` and `VERSION.json` using `tools/stamp_build.py`.
+New build ID: `366366b190edaa21`.
+
+## Windows installation
+
+1. Stop every TREBLO process and close old browser tabs.
+2. Extract this ZIP into a **new empty directory** (do not merge with old checkpoint).
+3. Use `.\run.ps1` from that directory (run `.\setup.ps1` on first launch if required).
+4. Open `http://127.0.0.1:8765/`; then hard-refresh with Ctrl+Shift+R.
+5. The UI must no longer show BUILD_MISMATCH, and `/api/health` must return build `366366b190edaa21`.
+6. If the port belongs to an old instance, run `.\diagnose.ps1`, terminate the old TREBLO process and retry.
+
+Frozen canonical MIDI/alignment modules were not modified. Native Windows and user-input acceptance still need actual machine-side verification.
